<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viktor Orbán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1963</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Viktor Orbán is a Hungarian politician, a founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidesz">Fidesz</a> party in 1988 and prime minister from 1998 to 2002 and again from 2010. His government used its two-thirds parliamentary majority to adopt a new constitution, the Fundamental Law of 2011, and his long dominance has shaped Hungarian politics in the 21st century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/viktor-orban.jpg" alt="Viktor Orbán" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The White House · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viktor_Orban_2025_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
